{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1483853-your-favorite-wta-tribe-book","id":1483853,"title":"Your favorite WtA tribe-book?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-13T02:21:32-07:00","id":1483853,"title":"Your favorite WtA tribe-book?","content":"OK, this thread suppose to cross &quot;Your favorite tribe&quot;-theme. Yet, I ask exactly in terms of: What tribe-book (of any edition) you see as the best writen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T04:53:39-07:00","id":1483855,"title":"","content":"Hmm. If forced to pick <i>one</i>, probably the revised Glasswalkers book.\ud83e\udd14","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T10:27:51-07:00","id":1483882,"title":"","content":"Red Talons revised. It was as impresive as book of the weaver","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T13:36:21-07:00","id":1483908,"title":"","content":"It's hard for me to pick one as well, simply because most of them were... just OK? The Tribes were probably one of the worst served splats by the old splat-book format. Even the decent Tribebooks could have easily been twice as long and come off as bare bones because Tribes are such big parts of Garou life and are largely fictional societies that you can't short cut as easily with real world references. I would say that Glass Walkers, Bone Gnawers, and Red Talons (rev for all of them, CoG are the only ones where I'd even begin to consider the 1e/2e books over the Rev ones) are probably the top simply because they have the least lifting to do in this regard. You come out of them with the most understanding of those Tribes cause they're, in many way, the easiest Tribes to understand (CoG should be, but for some reason the writing on them is always bad).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T14:24:21-07:00","id":1483919,"title":"","content":"I could think of a reason to go to the original run for Red Talons. It has to do with the author of RT Revised. Black Furies, too, accordingly.<br /> <br /> At any rate, I have to concur that bits of TBs can seem nice but a stand out TB as a whole tends to be rare. Shadow Lords Revised probably did more good things for them than the other books did for their tribes; it's primarily what I recall when thinking back 20 years to that run of books, but I'm also quite biased, as I ran out of gas about the S section and didn't get the Fianna book. Get of Fenris Revised also had the vitally important Fenrir Nazi purge, but the writer also had trouble differentiating the narrators, so it might have come across awkwardly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T05:07:00-07:00","id":1483980,"title":"","content":"Silent Striders revised is possibly the best written TB, simply because it goes DEEP into what makes a Strider.<br /> <br /> Shadow Lord Revised for the 'alpha myth is not real' part and generally explaining the tribes' functions beyond 'lol,manipulate.'<br /> <br /> Get of Fenris revised, because of the Nazi purge and taking away a lot of the old racist stuff.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T00:55:29-07:00","id":1484092,"title":"","content":"Shadow Lord Revised or Silent Strider Revised<br /> Tho' I must say the White Howler tibe book in WW20 turned to to be pretty nice too, tho' I kninda miss the old Howl-gifts (I know, I know, they were mostly a Talon-thing, but really, a Tribe that is literally called White HOWLERS!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}